# The agent image (apps/web/container/Dockerfile) is built with the REPO ROOT as
# its context, because it is a pnpm workspace package whose versions come from
# the root lockfile and catalog. Without this file that context is every
# node_modules, every build output and every tool cache in the tree — tens of
# gigabytes, which is not slow so much as a build that fails on disk.
#
# It lives at the root rather than beside the Dockerfile ON PURPOSE: BuildKit
# would find `apps/web/container/Dockerfile.dockerignore`, but the classic
# builder only ever reads `<context>/.dockerignore`, and `wrangler deploy` picks
# the builder, not us.
#
# The rule is "everything the image needs is a source file". Anything derived is
# rebuilt inside the image, so shipping a host's copy of it would at best waste
# the layer and at worst bake a macOS binary into a linux container.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.output
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/.wrangler
**/.tanstack
**/.next
**/.expo
**/coverage

.git
.github
.githooks

# Secrets never enter an image. `.dev.vars.example` is committed and harmless;
# the real files are not, and a build must not be the thing that copies them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.dev.vars

# Nothing outside apps/web/container is compiled into the daemon, but the whole
# tree is still needed for `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` to resolve the
# workspace. These are the parts that are neither: large binary assets and the
# desktop app's packaging inputs.
**/*.log
apps/desktop/build
apps/desktop/resources
apps/web/public
